==Battleground==
*5 [[Gabriel]]s spawn after 16.67 seconds<sup>500f</sup>, delay 6.67~10 seconds<sup>200f~300f</sup>.
*3 [[Heavenly Hippoe]]s spawn after 16.67 seconds<sup>500f</sup>, delay 16.67~20 seconds<sup>500f~600f</sup>.
*1 [[Angelic Gory]] spawns after 16.67 seconds<sup>500f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Head Rococo (Enemy)|Head Rococo]] spawns as the boss.
**1 [[Angelic Sleipnir]] spawns.
**Infinite [[Gabriel]]s spawn, delay 13.33~16.67 seconds<sup>400f~500f</sup>.
**2 [[Heavenly Hippoe]]s spawn, delay 0.07 seconds<sup>2f</sup>.
**3 [[Gabriel]]s spawn, delay 0.07 seconds<sup>2f</sup>.
**4 [[Otta-smack-u]]s spawn, delay 36.67 seconds<sup>1,100f</sup>.

==Strategy==
Head Rococo is at 100% magnification here, which means that they have 1,500,000 HP and 50,000 attack. They can potentially one-shot all of your units!! The peons here can make it easy for Head Rococo to advance, so be cautious. Using [[Rocker Cat (Rare Cat)|Ramen Cat]] as a meatshield is very useful here as everything (besides Otta-smack-u) is an [[:Category:Angel Enemies|Angel]]. Any other [[:Category:Anti-Angel Cats|Anti-Angel Cats]] can deal with the peons while any [[:Category:Long Distance Cats|Long Distance Cats]] such as [[Nerd Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Cyberpunk Cat]] can deal with Angelic Sleipnir and Head Rococo.

